### 6. Stability design

- Refresh requests are executed step by step to avoid long-term blocking of the interface and configuration web pages.
- Wi-Fi will automatically reconnect when disconnected. After successful reconnection, the time will be reset and refreshed.
- Use NTP to synchronize the time; do not initiate an HTTPS request before synchronizing the time
- Automatically back off for 5 minutes if authentication fails, and try again after 30 seconds if normal failure occurs.
- Give clear prompts when the platform limits traffic (HTTP 429)
- Read back and verify the configuration after it is written to avoid "prompt that the save was successful but it was not actually written"

