## 3. First-time configuration process

1. The device automatically enters the network distribution mode when it is powered on for the first time;
2. Use your mobile phone/computer to connect to the hotspot `StickS3-DS-XXXX` displayed on the screen, and the password will be displayed on the device screen;
3. Open the browser `http://192.168.4.1/`;
4. Enter the **6-digit administrative PIN** on the device screen to log in;
5. Fill in the following information:
- Wi-Fi name and password (2.4GHz only);
- DeepSeek API Key (for balance);
- Platform Token (for today’s usage);
- Time zone (default GMT+8);
- Refresh interval (default 60 seconds, adjustable 30–3600 seconds);
- screen brightness;
- Whether to automatically rotate and whether the horizontal screen direction is reversed;
6. Save and restart. The device will start displaying data after connecting to Wi-Fi.

> "Test Connection" requires the device to be connected to the Internet. In distribution mode, if the device is not connected to Wi-Fi, the test button will be automatically disabled; after saving and restarting, and the device being connected to the Internet, the configuration page can be opened through the device IP for testing.

### Platform Token Obtaining Method

1. Log in to `platform.deepseek.com` through your computer browser;
2. Press `F12` to open the developer tools and enter the Console;
3. Execute:

```js
copy(JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('userToken')).value)
```

4. Paste the clipboard content into the "Platform Token" input box on the web page.

Platform Token is equivalent to web page login credentials, please do not share them; you need to obtain it again after logging out of the platform, changing your password, or after Token expires, and the device will prompt "Token expired, please update."

